<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gongsun Shu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 36 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as White Emperor of Chengjia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gongsun Shu was a governor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> who, after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>, proclaimed himself emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a> in 25 CE, ruling the state of Chengjia as the White Emperor. He held the Sichuan basin for eleven years against the restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, until the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han">Emperor Guangwu</a> reached Chengdu in 36 CE; he was mortally wounded in the fighting and the city fell.</p></div>
